{"hits": {"hits": [{"links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9434?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A9434"}, "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Collins, John C."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "22", "artid": "1478", "year": 1980, "page_start": "1478", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "texkeys": ["Collins:1980ih"], "abstracts": [{"value": "A general method is explained for computing high-energy processes in gauge theories when \"Sudakov double logarithms\" are present. An expansion for the electron form factor in quantum electrodynamics is constructed; it gives the leading-logarithmic result of Sudakov, together with corrections to it to arbitrary logarithmic accuracy. The method can be applied to other processes, such as low-transverse-momentum parton phenomena, and form factors and elastic scattering of composite particles."}], "control_number": 9434, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.22.1478"}], "titles": [{"title": "Algorithm to Compute Corrections to the Sudakov Form-factor"}, {"title": "ALGORITHM TO COMPUTE CORRECTIONS TO THE SUDAKOV FORM-FACTOR"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "updated": "2023-03-06T21:27:57.760982+00:00", "id": "9434", "created": "1980-06-01T00:00:00+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Phys.Rev.D%2C22%2C1478&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,texkeys,abstracts.value,document_type,imprints,isbns,collaborations.value", "bib